    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scum_and_Villainy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy</a></i> </p><p>A Sniper Switch allows a Weapon that can be normally fired only in <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Autofire\" title=\"Autofire\">Autofire</a> mode (such as an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/E-Web_Repeating_Blaster\" title=\"E-Web Repeating Blaster\">E-Web Repeating Blaster</a>) to be used in Single-Fire mode. However, the Weapon no longer has reduced <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Autofire\" title=\"Autofire\">Autofire</a> penalties when <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Braced\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Braced\">Braced</a> because it is no longer an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Autofire\" title=\"Autofire\">Autofire</a>-only Weapon. Switching between the two firing modes is a&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Swift Action\">Swift Action</a>. </p>",
